MODIFICATIONS SINCE THE FORK

The fork is "detached": it does not track upstream releases, and its version
number (1.x) is intentionally independent of the upstream 0.3.x line. Relative
to upstream 0.3.4 the fork changes the following (measured by comparing this
repository's src/ tree against the src/ tree shipped in the upstream package;
see README "Differences from upstream" for the per-file counts):

  1. Human acceptance gate: a successful execution settlement parks the card in
     a new `review` column instead of declaring it done; a human moves it on
     (confirm/reject), and a rejected card returns to `todo` with the reason
     appended to its description.
  2. Card kinds: `once` / `recurring` / `interactive`, with settlement and
     scheduling behaviour derived from the kind, plus backward inference for
     cards written before the fork.
  3. Editable notes on executed cards: `description` stays editable after a run
     while title/prompt become read-only.
  4. Board lines: `line` / `seq` fields and a line view (cards grouped by work
     stream) alongside the status view.
  5. Settlement hardening: an `interrupted` outcome, stale "fake running"
     recovery, and a history-reading inspect path.
  6. Host-line portability: settings-service compatibility probing across host
     versions, and locally declared client runtime faces so the browser half no
     longer needs the dsh-* client packages at runtime.
  7. Sidebar entry rendering aligned with the host's own "new session" row.
  8. Localization copy carried in-tree instead of being read from the host
     locale service.

The full, file-by-file list lives in README.md / README.en.md under
"Differences from upstream".
